    "PipelineRefusal": {
      "description": "Typed refusals of the pipeline documents: bounds, formats and key identity\n(D2's document half), and `ForeignStore`, raised by `decode` for an\nenvelope of any other type. This is every refusal the leaf decides; a\nstore's identity and its schema epoch are not decided here, since this\ncrate owns no store, and belong to the organ that will admit these\ndocuments.\n\nSerialised externally tagged, serde's default for an enum: each variant is\na one-key map from the variant's name to its named fields, so `field` and\n`value` are on the wire under their own names and a reader of a refusal\ncarried over a wire reads the same parts a local caller matches on. No\nattribute buys that, which is why there is none: an internal or adjacent\ntag would move the fields under a content key without making any of them\nmore visible.",
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "FieldBound": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "actual": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "format": "uint32",
                  "minimum": 0
                },
                "field": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "limit": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "format": "uint32",
                  "minimum": 0
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "field",
                "limit",
                "actual"
              ]
            }
          },
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "FieldBound"
          ]
        },
